.LONG TERM...
Issued at 1200 PM PST Tue Nov 24 2026
(Thursday through next Monday)

The weather looks fairly quiet for the end of the week. Highs
generally stay near average in the low to mid-60s with lows in the
low-50s by the coast and bay, and in the 40s through the inland
valleys (perhaps a few 30s in the coldest spots).

The majority of GFS and ECMWF ensemble members show light
rainfall Sunday associated with a surface low pressure system
passing to the north. Both models also show the potential for a
more robust trough to move through sometime early next week
(around Tuesday), bringing the potential for more moderate/strong
rainfall.

