.AVIATION...
(00Z TAFS)
Issued at 351 PM PST Tue Nov 24 2026

High confidence of VFR conditions deteriorating to MVFR as the main
rain band moves in over the terminals tonight. Rain showers expected
overnight and will become scattered by early morning tomorrow. Winds
out of the SE will later shift E to NE by late morning. There is low
confidence on whether or not there will be gusty winds with this
cold frontal rain band tonight. Lower ceilings are expected to
persist into the afternoon hours tomorrow hovering at VFR/MVFR
ceiling heights.

Vicinity of SFO...VFR conditions will start deteriorating to MVFR once the rain
starts to move over the forecast area. Rain showers are expected to
develop around 05Z and will become scattered in the early morning
hours. There is low confidence regarding wind direction and speed.
The winds have been more consistently out of the east, but a
southerly shift is likely once the rain band arrives tonight. There
is low confidence on whether or not we will see any gusty conditions
with the arrival of the rain band tonight, but given the decrease in
storm severity over the last 48 hours, the chances are most likely
low.

SFO Bridge Approach...Similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...Some broken clouds sticking around with VFR conditions through the
TAF period. Winds are variable at MRY and out of the N at SNS. Both
sites should see winds increase a bit and shift to SE as a cold
front approaches tonight. Light rain showers tonight but confidence
is low in seeing any rain.

